WEBVTT

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.190
All right!

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:08.990
I think this is good.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:17.120
I revised it a little. How's this?

00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:19.770
Looks good.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:21.350
Oh my!

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:23.640
What a nice cycling jersey!

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:26.250
Great job, Ami!

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.750
With this, our team jerseys are going to be...

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:43.530
Now, we just wait for them!

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:19.520
Oh, what a nice day!

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.250
You're awfully dirty.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:32.500
Well, I rely on you a lot for going to school and work.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.130
Okay, then!

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.320
You should always want your beloved bike
to be sparkling clean, right?

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.150
Okay, let's do it!

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.780
It feels so great to see the grime steadily coming off!

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.610
I'll keep going at this pace!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:23.510
Okay, I think that'll do.

00:03:23.510 --> 00:03:26.510
Finally, just rinse off with water.

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:27.800
Oh boy...

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:31.110
This is pretty hard on the back.

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:40.920
After I'm done with Ponta-kun,
I'll make you all clean too, so just wait a bit, okay?

00:03:41.490 --> 00:03:43.670
Our team jerseys are arriving soon.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:46.680
So let's make ourselves nice and
shiny for a fresh new start!

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:50.620
Here goes!

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.250
Huh?

00:03:55.080 --> 00:03:56.380
How come?

00:03:57.020 --> 00:03:58.880
I turned the faucet on.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.920
Is the hose tangled somewhere?

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.350
Whoa, that surprised me.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:14.190
I'm soaking wet.

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:16.980
Oh well, it's hot today.

00:04:17.370 --> 00:04:19.860
I can cool down together with Ponta-kun this way.

00:04:19.860 --> 00:04:21.680
It's perfect.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.020
I'm home.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:25.240
Welcome home, Emi.

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.120
Come on, Onee-chan...

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.370
Huh? What is it?

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:30.990
Look at yourself!

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.260
Hello...

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:46.370
Ah, Aoi-san, hello!

00:04:46.370 --> 00:04:47.640
Aoi-chan!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.360
Why's your hair wet?

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:54.140
Well, I was cleaning Ponta-kun and...

00:04:54.140 --> 00:04:56.650
Okay, I get it.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:59.450
Next is your road bike?

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:00.610
Yes!

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:03.270
What's your usual maintenance routine?

00:05:03.270 --> 00:05:05.870
I wash and oil the bikes.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:11.410
That reminds me, you haven't had an initial inspection since the purchase, have you?

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.160
Maybe you should take it to the shop and get it checked.

00:05:15.490 --> 00:05:18.380
Initial... inspection?

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:22.990
I highly recommend this new product.

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.420
Oh, welcome-paca!

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.180
Ah, Hinako-san and Yayoi-san!

00:05:27.530 --> 00:05:29.700
Oh, Ami! Aoi!

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.280
Hello.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.990
Came to buy something?

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:36.310
No, I was thinking of having my road bike checked.

00:05:36.310 --> 00:05:42.390
I figured it would be a good idea for Ami to see what professional maintenance looks like.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.070
It'll be my pleasure-paca!

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.880
All right, I'll take a look-paca.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.830
Thank you very much!

00:05:57.680 --> 00:06:00.470
Hmm, this chain is...

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.590
Is something wrong?

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.730
I'll take a closer look-paca.

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:08.970
There's not enough lubricant, so there's no oil film-paca.

00:06:09.490 --> 00:06:13.300
There's more resistance if you don't oil the chain.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:15.050
That's absolutely right-paca.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.350
Okay, "not enough lubrication is bad"...!

00:06:17.350 --> 00:06:21.000
This is how you lubricate the chain-paca.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:25.110
And be careful that you don't get oil on any other part-paca.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:31.240
The derailleur and brake pivot too.
Only apply oil to the section that moves-paca.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:37.680
And finish by wiping off the excess oil with a towel.

00:06:37.680 --> 00:06:40.120
And... "wipe off the oil."

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:42.540
Okay, all done-paca!

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:46.300
Oh, the sound is...

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.510
Can you tell, Ami?
It's quieter, right?

00:06:49.510 --> 00:06:54.190
That's proof that it's turning more smoothly than before.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:57.940
You'll have less friction, so the ride will be even more comfortable.

00:06:57.940 --> 00:06:58.890
I see!

00:06:59.500 --> 00:07:02.150
Next, I'll check the gear changer-paca.

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.190
The cable is a little stretched-paca.

00:07:13.830 --> 00:07:17.650
Have you noticed a slight delay
when you change gears-paca?

00:07:17.650 --> 00:07:20.370
Now that you mention it, I have!

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:24.010
Brand new cables always stretch a little-paca.

00:07:24.010 --> 00:07:28.540
So this is a situation where
you use this adjuster bolt-paca.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:29.790
Okay...

00:07:29.790 --> 00:07:34.220
And if you still hear the chain
rubbing after adjusting with this...

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:37.710
use a screw driver to turn these two screws-paca.

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:40.070
This is the top adjuster bolt...

00:07:40.070 --> 00:07:41.960
and here's the lower adjuster bolt.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:47.820
Then look straight from the back to make sure the derailleur hanger isn't bent-paca.

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:52.180
Ami-chan, what's the matter?

00:07:52.180 --> 00:07:55.280
I'm sorry... I can't follow you at all.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.820
I'll check for you until you learn.

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:01.080
Just bring it by anytime-paca.

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:04.080
Thank you so much.

00:08:05.010 --> 00:08:07.780
Finally, we check the brake very carefully.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:12.090
If there are any irregularities,
change the brakeshoe. And that's it-paca.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:16.040
Okay, thank you!

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:23.310
I'll be able to ride with more confidence now that I know these things.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:27.660
Once you're used to it,
you can do the simple things yourself.

00:08:27.660 --> 00:08:33.050
With proper maintenance,
your bike will last a long time,

00:08:33.050 --> 00:08:36.370
and you'll avoid running into trouble on the road.

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:39.740
Right! I'll work hard so I can learn to do it myself.

00:08:39.740 --> 00:08:43.250
Ami-chan... Do you know what this is?

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:44.370
Huh?

00:08:44.700 --> 00:08:46.880
It's a chain cleaner.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:51.750
This makes cleaning the hardest part of the chain a cinch.

00:08:51.750 --> 00:08:54.430
Wow, this is really useful!

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.700
It sure is!

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:01.400
And if you're going to do it yourself, proper equipment is a must!

00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.910
Wow!

00:09:02.910 --> 00:09:05.850
But do you really need all this?

00:09:05.850 --> 00:09:10.640
Besides that, a work stand like this is most desirable.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.280
W-Wait, Yayoi-san!
I don't have room for all this!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:16.780
If you purchased all this...

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:22.040
141,020 yen-paca!

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:28.090
Impossible!

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:31.050
I'm home.

00:09:31.870 --> 00:09:33.310
Welcome home, Onee-chan.

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:34.910
That was delivered for you.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.720
Thank you!

00:09:49.600 --> 00:09:51.690
It's here at last!

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.580
All right...!

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:07.830
These are...

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:10.580
our team jerseys!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.200
I'm so...

00:10:18.190 --> 00:10:20.040
excited!

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:26.910
Mom?

00:10:29.070 --> 00:10:31.790
Joyful moments you enjoy for yourself turn into...

00:10:31.790 --> 00:10:36.110
regretful memories that you want to stop and erase
the moment someone catches you...

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:37.490
Do you understand, Emi?

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:38.440
Yes.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:41.240
So at times like this...

00:10:41.240 --> 00:10:44.370
we just pretend we didn't see anything. For their sake.

00:10:44.370 --> 00:10:45.500
Okay.

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:10.020
What's the matter, Ami?

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:11.620
Um...

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:15.400
I'm so happy about the fact that we're wearing matching jerseys!

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:17.820
It's a great design.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:21.410
You can recognize it right away from a distance too.

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:25.350
The goddess on the back is so cute.

00:11:25.350 --> 00:11:28.540
I can't believe this is your first design.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.410
Thanks, Ami!

00:11:38.120 --> 00:11:40.370
Okay, shall we get going?

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:41.270
Yes!

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:50.310
If only Saki-san were here,
we'd have the entire Fortuna team.

00:11:50.310 --> 00:11:53.160
I'm sure there'll be another opportunity.

00:11:53.160 --> 00:11:53.940
You're right!

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:56.690
Okay!

00:11:56.690 --> 00:12:01.650
Team Fortuna's first ride is to Nikko's Iroha Hill!

00:12:01.650 --> 00:12:02.820
Let's go!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:03.560
Yes!

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:31.770
Thanks to the maintenance we did,
the ride is so comfortable!

00:12:35.470 --> 00:12:37.980
And cycling in matching jerseys...

00:12:38.620 --> 00:12:40.630
is so much fun!

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:45.580
Hey, caught up already?

00:13:45.580 --> 00:13:50.110
She conquered Yabitsu Pass.
This is nothing for her now.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:55.600
Well, it was tough going at times,
but I managed somehow.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:58.840
We're close to the turnaround point,
let's replenish ourselves.

00:14:07.610 --> 00:14:08.950
Saki-san!

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:13.870
Ami? What a coincidence, meeting you out here!

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:16.020
Yeah, it is a coincidence.

00:14:16.020 --> 00:14:20.440
We sent you a message, but you didn't even reply.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.630
You didn't even read it in the first place.

00:14:22.630 --> 00:14:24.570
Sorry, sorry!

00:14:24.570 --> 00:14:27.630
When I'm riding alone,
I don't check my phone.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:33.350
We should've asked about your schedule too, Saki-chan.

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:34.410
No use.

00:14:34.410 --> 00:14:39.390
Unless she's on a Brevet,
she changes course on a whim.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:42.220
Isn't that what riding alone is all about?

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:46.740
Saki-san, you wore our jersey!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:49.380
Yes, it's really nice.

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:51.810
We didn't see you on the way...

00:14:51.810 --> 00:14:55.290
Did you leave Nikko Station really early?

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:56.920
Nope.

00:14:56.920 --> 00:15:01.040
I went cycling in Gunma yesterday, then spent a night in Katashina Village,

00:15:01.040 --> 00:15:03.790
and went through Konsei Pass to get here.

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:06.460
All the way from... Gunma?

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:12.680
But still, this is Team Fortuna's first event...

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:16.810
and we're celebrating with plain old curry?!

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:18.810
Isn't that fine, so long as it's a good memory?

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:23.210
Yeah! The curry here is great.

00:15:23.210 --> 00:15:26.320
We made it here, let's eat up!

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.560
Thank you for waiting.

00:15:40.270 --> 00:15:42.230
This curry is delicious!

00:15:42.230 --> 00:15:43.120
Yeah!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:55.640
The taste of this curry...

00:15:55.640 --> 00:15:58.140
is something I'll never forget!

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.260
Don't go too fast, Saki.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:09.030
I know!

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:13.870
Almost time for a rest stop!

00:16:15.570 --> 00:16:20.010
Um... I'm not tired at all
since we've been going downhill, so...

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:24.290
There are sudden curves,
so we have to be careful.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:28.040
Being almost too careful is the way to go.

00:16:28.040 --> 00:16:30.460
Okay, I see.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:34.760
By the way, Ami, you don't grip the drops even when going downhill?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:37.680
Well, the posture gets uncomfortable, so...

00:16:37.680 --> 00:16:40.820
That... can be really dangerous, you know?

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.220
Really?

00:16:43.880 --> 00:16:48.350
She sure talks big, but she's the one who went flying because of it.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:49.440
Hey, Hinako!

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.450
Huh? Flying?

00:16:55.230 --> 00:16:59.260
Sharing experiences is important.
Tell them what happened.

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.460
I guess it can't be helped...

00:17:04.590 --> 00:17:09.460
It happened when I first started riding road bikes.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:15.970
Wow! It's beautiful!

00:17:15.970 --> 00:17:20.470
I wasn't used to the
forward leaning posture on my road bike.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:30.940
Huh?

00:17:36.880 --> 00:17:37.960
I'm going...

00:17:39.200 --> 00:17:40.400
to die.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:45.960
And I went flying through the sky.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.330
I was so young then...

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:53.590
What? And were you okay?

00:17:54.430 --> 00:17:58.420
Luckily, the leaves I fell onto acted as a cushion.

00:17:58.420 --> 00:18:01.030
So I wasn't hurt badly.

00:18:01.030 --> 00:18:02.290
Amazing!

00:18:02.290 --> 00:18:03.700
It was a miracle.

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:07.880
I felt my heart sink because
I thought my bicycle was wrecked.

00:18:04.800 --> 00:18:10.360
Ah, my bike! My bike! My bike! My bike!

00:18:07.880 --> 00:18:10.360
You should worry about your body first!

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:14.890
It was brand new!
Wouldn't you cry if it turned to scrap?!

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:17.320
I get how you felt, but...

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:21.070
You can buy another bicycle,
but you only have one life.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:26.990
Well, my bike was stuck in a tree,
so it just had a little scratch.

00:18:26.990 --> 00:18:28.830
You were really fortunate.

00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:34.000
But you understand that I really could have died, right?

00:18:35.590 --> 00:18:39.340
So when you go downhill,
your hands should be on the drops.

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.650
Promise me that!

00:18:41.650 --> 00:18:46.060
It's so much more convincing when you say it, Saki.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:51.570
Shut up! You're the one who made me tell them!

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.230
Oh yeah...

00:18:54.230 --> 00:18:56.230
What is it, Ami?

00:18:56.230 --> 00:19:01.490
You fell on the way down, right, Saki-san?
Where was that?

00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:05.490
Right over there. On that ledge.

00:19:12.500 --> 00:19:14.670
I'm amazed you survived.

00:19:16.360 --> 00:19:18.010
I know!

00:19:18.010 --> 00:19:20.200
That's for sure.

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:23.370
In order to teach the importance of breaking,

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:27.520
this incident should be passed down
for generations to come.

00:19:29.190 --> 00:19:30.520
I'm sorry.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:32.720
Please forgive me.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.940
Ami, your pace was better than usual today.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.030
Was it?

00:19:47.790 --> 00:19:50.040
Maybe it's because I was wearing this jersey...

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:55.380
It was tough, but I was able to
put in more effort than usual!

00:19:57.480 --> 00:19:58.260
Ami...

00:20:01.710 --> 00:20:03.390
Oh, my...

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:08.280
After hearing that, I have to admit that
making matching jerseys was worth it.

00:20:08.280 --> 00:20:11.640
You're right.
Anyway, it's about time I got going...

00:20:11.640 --> 00:20:14.640
Saki-san, you're cycling home?

00:20:14.640 --> 00:20:15.810
No.

00:20:15.810 --> 00:20:18.890
I want to cycle to Inawashiro Lake tomorrow.

00:20:18.890 --> 00:20:22.820
So I'll probably to go to Utsunomiya today and spend the night.

00:20:22.820 --> 00:20:25.920
You're cycling that far tomorrow too?!

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:29.070
Once you're used to it, this is normal.

00:20:29.070 --> 00:20:30.830
See you!

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:33.990
She's amazing.

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:40.120
Saki-san's always riding,
does she still go to class?

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.590
Well, that's Saki. Don't worry about her.

00:20:46.560 --> 00:20:51.510
But I wonder how many kilos
she's ridden yesterday and today.

00:20:51.510 --> 00:20:52.880
Probably...

00:20:52.880 --> 00:20:55.660
around 300 kilos all together.

00:20:56.480 --> 00:21:01.360
Hey, the flèche you want to participate in is even longer than that.

00:21:01.960 --> 00:21:04.880
I know that, but...

00:21:04.880 --> 00:21:07.580
How do I even prepare to ride that far?

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:09.460
Don't have a clue?

00:21:09.460 --> 00:21:13.270
Then why don't we enter a cycling event next time?

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:15.120
Cycling event?

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:17.180
There are all kinds...

00:21:17.180 --> 00:21:19.060
Let's see...

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:22.220
How about the Azumino Autumn Ride?

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:26.010
Sounds great!
If I remember right, we can enter as a team.

00:21:26.640 --> 00:21:28.260
As a team?

00:21:29.840 --> 00:21:31.520
We can ride together?

00:21:31.520 --> 00:21:33.120
Well, Ami?

00:21:33.630 --> 00:21:39.190
Umm... I don't quite understand...
but I think I'd like to try.

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:40.900
Okay, it's decided!

00:21:40.900 --> 00:21:41.530
Yes!

00:21:41.530 --> 00:21:44.910
So for our first event... we'll break 100 kilos!

00:21:45.780 --> 00:21:47.220
100 kilos?!

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:33.460
I'm so glad they liked the team jerseys!

00:23:33.460 --> 00:23:36.650
It'd be great if our team's bond becomes even stronger!

00:23:36.650 --> 00:23:41.280
I want to try this cycling event...
but 100 kilos sounds daunting!

00:23:41.280 --> 00:23:44.980
Next time on Long Riders: "An Expanding World."
